The publish gate. While this file exists the release workflow tags nothing.

yze-md-markup has never been pushed anywhere. It was built locally, and its name
is provisional — the owner may rename it before any of it is published, and a
module path is the one thing a rename cannot take back once the proxy has seen
it. proxy.golang.org is first-write-wins and permanent: the first fetch of any
version caches that tree's zip forever and sum.golang.org records its hash, so a
tag cut before the name is settled is a tag this module carries for good.

So the hold stays until publication is a decision rather than a side effect of a
push: the name is chosen, the leak vet passes over the whole tree and its full
history, an adversarial round returns clean, and only then is a single v0.1.0 cut
deliberately from a tree somebody chose.

Removing this file IS the act of publishing. Do not remove it to quiet a
workflow.
